  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\theta )]}^{6}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\theta )]}^{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-6$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\theta )]}^{-6}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-6\\theta )\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-6\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(6\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(6\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
